I propose a simple, twofold solution.  For the #ifdef HARD option,
I suggest that the old technique of simply polymorphing the top object
of the "poly-pile" should be used, #else no change from the current
code.  This way, if you want the easy-to-win version you just compile
it without HARD.  Sheesh, you guys, I can remember when polymorph wands
didn't work on objects at all!  I like to polymorph objects too, but
polymorphing hundreds of different objects at one time is obscene.

